{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787306094635873001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"surprised-convincing-gopher","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f0222125d0adafa41c29b06b65649fe20fa904d7b75ab625f3da8d8c64373be5","event_uuid":"a115b55b-d508-49f5-b5a6-3ed9768c655f","position":{"commit_sha":"2e1d59e67af52c8e3fd16f3b11836cebc715334e","position":"1787301098281874001-a115b55b-d508-49f5-b5a6-3ed9768c655f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e1b3a6cadf178246639e2a6974efdb5fc37ff6c7686bbbff1634c1b5c62cfff4","event_uuid":"917b3813-e853-4b58-a786-596901ad2d52","position":{"commit_sha":"3541fff3a7b472e62dd0799e49101aa56f12bf9d","position":"1787301108330482001-917b3813-e853-4b58-a786-596901ad2d52"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787301098281874001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"917b3813-e853-4b58-a786-596901ad2d52","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ff2e-339c-237e-4519"}],"description":"## Problem\n`KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` in `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` is fail-open in a SECOND, opposite\ndirection from bug `defiable-distortive-pinniped` (ff2e): nothing validates a row against the\ntree, so a row whose helper no longer exists is kept forever with no diagnostic.\n\n**MEASURED: 4 of the 11 current rows are ghosts** — `_rebar_env`, `_env_int`, `_str_pref`,\n`_int_pref` have NO `def` site anywhere under `src/rebar`. The RP-04 config-ownership cutover\ndrained them (`269b4d5678`, `d361eb28e4`).\n\n## Why this is a real defect and not cosmetic\nA ghost row is the visible half of a rename that silently dropped keys. `269b4d5678` deleted\n`def _str_pref` and introduced `_gate_str_pref` in its place WITHOUT renaming the row. The\nresult: the row went stale (matching nothing) and `REBAR_GATE_REF` / `REBAR_GATE_SOURCE`\nsilently vanished from `docs/env-vars.md`, where they stayed missing from 2026-08-18 until\nff2e. A gate that fails when a row stops matching would have caught that rename AT the rename,\nnaming the exact cause, instead of leaving it to be found by census two months later.\n\nff2e closes the \"helper with no row\" direction (an unregistered parameter-keyed helper now\naborts the scan). This ticket is the mirror: \"row with no helper\".\n\n## Sketches (decide on evidence)\n- Fail closed on a row with no matching `def` under the scan root — symmetric with ff2e, and\n  it directly detects the rename-without-updating-the-row case.\n- Watch for the false-positive risk: a helper legitimately defined outside the scan root, or\n  a row deliberately kept for a helper about to land. If that case is real, the exemption\n  must be explicit rather than a silent skip.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` row with no matching helper definition under the scan root\n      produces a loud failure naming the stale row, proven by a test that FAILS against\n      today's generator.\n- [ ] The four ghost rows above are removed (or the gate is made to accept them with a\n      recorded, explicit reason).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the full unit sweep stay green, and\n      `docs/env-vars.md` does not shrink.\n- [ ] `scan()` keeps its 2-tuple arity — `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` unpacks it and\n      imports `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` directly, so a stricter table affects that consumer and\n      `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py` must stay green.\n\n## Provenance\nFound by census while fixing ff2e (defiable-distortive-pinniped). Deliberately NOT folded into\nthat change: ff2e's diff is scoped to its proven root cause (helper-with-no-row), and the\nghost rows cause no key loss today, so fixing them there would have widened the diff past the\nmechanism under proof.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"84c7-486f-9a13-4c3f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS keeps ghost rows for helpers that no longer exist","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a115b55b-d508-49f5-b5a6-3ed9768c655f","917b3813-e853-4b58-a786-596901ad2d52"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787306094635873001,"uuid":"4b46cb9b-7294-422c-8ca8-f065ce3dcd33"}